  "content_text": "\r\n    \r\n        \r\n    \r\n    \r\n        \n            Manhattan Active SCALE Documentation\r\n        How to: Use Swagger\r\n    \r\n    \r\n         \n                Collapse All\n                Expand All\n            \r\n        View with Navigation Tools\r\n    \r\n    \r\n    \r\n    \r\n    \r\n        The Swagger consumes SCALE REST APIs and provides a UI interface to invoke and see the response from the APIs.\r\n\r\n\r\n     Launch Swagger\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    To launch Swagger, browse to URL https://environment.domain.com/ilsIntegrationServices/swagger. The API documentation will be available in swagger UI as shown below. Login to SCALE web screen prior to launching Swagger. Also, use the same host name in the swagger URL as used for launching the SCALE web screen.\r\n\r\n    Swagger consumes the same authorization token generated for the SCALE application during the login process.  Therefore, while launching the Swagger application or invoking Web API using Swagger, if an “Invalid token” error occurs, refresh the SCALE application and perform the authorization steps.Refresh the Swagger application as well. To consume Swagger using other valid token pass token in Authorization header in request as \r\n\r\n    Authorization: Bearer <token>\r\n\r\n    New token can be passed or can be changed in the Swagger application using “Authorize” button available within the application.Detailed Swagger documentation about APIs is available in JSON format at the doc URL. As it's available here at https://env1.manh.com/ILSIntegrationServices/swagger/docs/V1\r\n\r\n    \r\n\r\n     \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n     Invoke API using Swagger\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n     \r\n\r\n    REST APIs can be invoked using Swagger ,and to invoke specific API, follow the steps below:\r\n\r\n     \r\n\r\n    1.  Select the API. e.g.  \"GetScreenflows\".\r\n\r\n    2.  API documentation provides role required to execute API.\r\n\r\n    3.  Click on \"Try it Out\". The \"Execute\" button should be visible by now.\r\n\r\n    4.  Pass required parameters to API. if any. Click \"Execute\".\r\n\r\n    5.  API response can be seen in the ‘Responses’ section. An API sample response is provided prior to execution.\r\n\r\n     \r\n\r\n     \r\n\r\n\r\n \n            \n            \r\n        \r\n    \r\n    \r\n        \n  ©2026 Manhattan Associates. All Rights Reserved.\n\r\n    \r\n    \r\n\r\n    \r\n    \r\n    \r\n",
  "search_text": "\r\n    \n\r\n        \r\n    \n\r\n    \n\r\n        \n            \nManhattan Active SCALE Documentation\n\r\n        \n\nHow to: Use Swagger\n\n\r\n    \n\r\n    \n\r\n         \n                Collapse All\n                Expand All\n            \r\n        View with Navigation Tools\r\n    \n\r\n    \r\n    \r\n    \r\n    \n\r\n        \nThe Swagger consumes SCALE REST APIs and provides a UI interface to invoke and see the response from the APIs.\n\r\n\r\n\n\r\n     Launch Swagger\r\n\n\r\n\r\n\n\r\n    \nTo launch Swagger, browse to URL https://environment.domain.com/ilsIntegrationServices/swagger. The API documentation will be available in swagger UI as shown below. Login to SCALE web screen prior to launching Swagger. Also, use the same host name in the swagger URL as used for launching the SCALE web screen.\n\r\n\r\n    \nSwagger consumes the same authorization token generated for the SCALE application during the login process.  Therefore, while launching the Swagger application or invoking Web API using Swagger, if an “Invalid token” error occurs, refresh the SCALE application and perform the authorization steps.Refresh the Swagger application as well. To consume Swagger using other valid token pass token in Authorization header in request as \n\r\n\r\n    \nAuthorization: Bearer <token>\n\r\n\r\n    \nNew token can be passed or can be changed in the Swagger application using “Authorize” button available within the application.\nDetailed Swagger documentation about APIs is available in JSON format at the doc URL. As it's available here at https://env1.manh.com/ILSIntegrationServices/swagger/docs/V1\r\n\r\n    \n\n\r\n\r\n    \n \n\r\n\n\r\n\r\n\n\r\n     Invoke API using Swagger\r\n\n\r\n\r\n\n\r\n    \n \n\r\n\r\n    \nREST APIs can be invoked using Swagger ,and to invoke specific API, follow the steps below:\n\r\n\r\n    \n \n\r\n\r\n    \n1.  Select the API. e.g.  \"GetScreenflows\".\n\r\n\r\n    \n2.  API documentation provides role required to execute API.\n\r\n\r\n    \n3.  Click on \"Try it Out\". The \"Execute\" button should be visible by now.\n\r\n\r\n    \n4.  Pass required parameters to API. if any. Click \"Execute\".\n\r\n\r\n    \n5.  API response can be seen in the ‘Responses’ section. An API sample response is provided prior to execution.\n\r\n\r\n    \n \n\r\n\r\n    \n \n\r\n\n\r\n\r\n\n \n\n            \n            \r\n        \r\n    \n\r\n    \n\r\n        \n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n©2026 Manhattan Associates. All Rights Reserved.\n\n\r\n    \n\r\n    \r\n\r\n    \r\n    \r\n    \r\n",
